    board: file CF-078/CF-079/CF-080 — the node identity path has three measured gaps: the manifest writer contradicts its spec and no shipped adapter can reach it, the layer table names capabilities no code establishes, and --apply builds the workspace after the bus layer failed. Addresses CF-078.
    
    CF-078 (P3) specs/NODE.md:7-16 requires bus.agent_id and harness.version; scripts/project-node.sh:255-266 writes neither, takes bus.base from CRIER_BASE (one hit in the whole repo: that line) while layer 00 measures CRIER_URL, and builds repo.path as '/home/'+$USER+'/repo' instead of the path the run used. Unreachable in practice: hermes --apply fails on python 3.14.9, opencode --apply is refused as an unmeasured ladder, claude-code is absent, and selftest only runs scoped (layer 90 -> SKIP), so node.json is produced by no shipped path and exercised by no test.
    
    CF-079 (P4) specs/NODE.md:29 and :31 claim layer 30 establishes 'a pull worker' and layer 90 'one round trip whose digest is recomputed on the control host'; the script checks only file existence/mode at 30 and only writes the manifest at 90. No row owned the spec claim (CF-004 owns building the round trip, CF-068 the file-existence weakness).
    
    CF-080 (P4) measured this tick at ac30ceb: the documented --apply run printed 'FAIL crier_identity — absent' at layer 30 and then cloned, 'PASS repo_clone — <tmp>/repo @ 6bb5af7', leaving $HOME/repo behind. AGENTS.md rule 9 forbids exactly that node; only the disk-admission guard refuses to continue, although the layer-00 comment claims apply refuses immediately.
    
